<section data-specimen="type">
  <h3>Type scale</h3>
  <p class="hint">
    Five sizes on an alternating 1.33 / 1.5 ratio. Every line box is a whole
    number of lines, so a heading never lands the type under it off the grid.
  </p>
  <%# The rung, the number of lines it is set on, and the face for the ratio
      of the two. Every leading is a whole number of lines, which is the grid
      in step; the face puts each baseline on the under edge of its line,
      which is the grid registered. %>
  <% { 1 => [ "--line", "--face-200", "Labels and metadata" ], 2 => [ "--line", "--face-150", "Body copy" ],
       3 => [ "--line-2", "--face-200", "Section" ], 4 => [ "--line-2", "--face-150", "Subhead" ],
       5 => [ "--line-3", "--face-150", "Page title" ] }.each do |step, (leading, face, name)| %>
    <p data-size="<%= step %>" style="font-family: var(<%= face %>), var(--font-family); font-size: var(--size-<%= step %>); line-height: var(<%= leading %>)">
      <%= name %> — <code>--size-<%= step %></code> on <code><%= leading %></code> in <code><%= face %></code>
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <h4>Registers</h4>
  <p>Body. The measure holds prose to three fields, which is where it stops rather than where the window does.</p>
  <p class="quiet">Quiet. This is secondary.</p>
  <p class="micro">Micro. Labels, metadata, captions — never capitals.</p>
  <p class="hint">Hint. What a field needs said about it.</p>
  <p class="tabular">Tabular 0123456789 — figures read down a column.</p>
  <p><%= link_to "A link keeps its underline", "#type", class: "link-quiet" %> and a button does not.</p>
</section>
